    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Property Partners McDonnell are delighted to introduce this Charming 3 Bedroom Detached bungalow, nestled on approx. c. 0.4 Acre (c.1,400 sq.m) in the peaceful countryside of Rahanine, just minutes from Rochfortbridge village.\r\nSet amidst beautifully mature gardens with established trees, hedging and shrubbery, this inviting home enjoys exceptional privacy while offering excellent connectivity to Mullingar, the M4 motorway and surrounding towns. The generous site provides an ideal environment for family living, outdoor enjoyment and potential future expansion.\r\nInternally, the property offers bright, well-proportioned accommodation with a warm and welcoming atmosphere throughout. A spacious entrance hall leads to a comfortable sitting room featuring attractive wall panelling and a solid fuel stove, creating the perfect focal point for relaxing evenings. A separate study provides an ideal work-from-home space and flows seamlessly into the open-plan kitchen and dining area, complete with recessed lighting, a Stanley range with back boiler and direct access to the rear patio and garden.\r\nThe accommodation is completed by 3 generous bedrooms, including a master bedroom with ensuite shower room, together with a well-appointed family bathroom. Tasteful décor and practical layout combine to create a home that is both comfortable and functional.\r\nOutside, the property boasts a substantial garage attached suitable for workshop use, storage or potential conversion, together with a separate turf shed and ample off-street parking via a hardcore driveway and gated entrance.\r\nLocated within walking distance of Rochfortbridge village, St. Joseph's Secondary School, local sporting facilities and bus services to Dublin and beyond, this attractive residence combines the tranquillity of rural living with the convenience of excellent local amenities.\r\nOffering space, privacy and tremendous potential in a highly sought-after location"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall \r\n3.24m x 2.63m  \r\nLaminate flooring. Attic access. Walk-In Hot press. \r\n\r\nLiving Room \r\n3.73m x 4.38m  \r\nLaminate flooring. Wall panelling, TV point. Solid fuel stove. \r\n\r\nStudy/Office \r\n2.63m x 2.97m \r\nLaminate flooring. Wall panelling. Phone & internet point. Archway through to dining area. \r\n\r\nKitchen/Dining Room\r\n3.49m x 6.37m  \r\nLino flooring. Recessed lighting. Open-plan. Door to rear garden. Stanley solid fuel stove with back boiler. \r\n\r\nMain Family Bathroom \r\n2.27m x 2.15m  \r\nLino flooring. Timber panel ceiling. With W.C., W.H.B., bath& electric shower.\r\n\r\nBedroom 1 \r\n2.40m x 3.28m  \r\nLaminate flooring. Coving. \r\n\r\nBedroom 2 Master\r\n4.11m x 3.55m  \r\nLaminate flooring. Coving. \r\n\r\nEnsuite \r\n1.27m x 1.10m  \r\nTiled floor & walls. With W.C., W.H.B & pump shower. \r\n\r\nBedroom 3 \r\n4.09m x 2.43m  \r\nLaminate flooring. Coving. Fitted wardrobe. \r\n\r\nGarage \r\n10.43m x 3.81m"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Dual Central Heating (with both oil fired & solid fuel) \r\nExtremely Bright Spacious House \r\nOn approx. c. 0.4 Acre (c.1,400 sq.m)Acres of matured ground\r\nMains water& Septic tank sewerage \r\nGenerous garage attached (ideal for workshop /or conversion  \r\nMature private rear garden \r\nNot overlooked \r\nGated side entrance  \r\nHardcore driveway with ample on-site parking  \r\nMature trees & shrubbery  \r\nLarge turf shed \r\nAmple space to extend \r\nGlazed windows\r\nPatio to rear \r\nLocated beside bus stop for Dublin City & Local Town Link  \r\nAdjacent to St. Josephs Secondary school\r\nMinutes’ walk to Rochfortbridge village & Local GAA Club \r\nMullingar 15km, Tullamore 28km, 30 minutes Athlone"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "BER Details",
        "SortOrder": 4,
        "Content": "BER: D"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Directions",
        "SortOrder": 5,
        "Content": "Google Maps: N91 W3P0\r\nNestled in the heart of County Westmeath, Rochfortbridge is a welcoming and well-established village that offers the perfect blend of rural charm and modern convenience. \r\nIdeally positioned along the N52 and just minutes from the M4 motorway, it provides excellent connectivity to Mullingar, Tullamore, Athlone and Dublin, making it an ideal location for commuters and families alike.\r\nThe village boasts a wide range of local amenities including schools, shops, cafés, sporting facilities and a thriving GAA club, all contributing to its strong sense of community. Surrounded by picturesque countryside and scenic walking routes, residents can enjoy a relaxed lifestyle while remaining close to all essential services.\r\nWith its friendly atmosphere, convenient transport links and excellent local amenities, Rochfortbridge continues to be one of Westmeath's most attractive locations for those seeking quality country living without compromising on accessibility."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Viewing Details",
        "SortOrder": 6,
        "Content": "Viewing strictly by appointment only"
      }
